content.thinking:
The problem is clear - the footer has `z-index: 20` which is higher than the sticky section z-index values (1-5), so when you scroll down, the footer covers the kontak section. I need to either:
1. Lower the footer z-index to something below 5 (but above 0)
2. Or increase the z-index of the kontak sticky section

Looking at the sticky section z-index rules:
```css
.sticky-section:nth-of-type(1) { z-index: 1; }
.sticky-section:nth-of-type(2) { z-index: 2; }
.sticky-section:nth-of-type(3) { z-index: 3; }
.sticky-section:nth-of-type(4) { z-index: 4; }
.sticky-section:nth-of-type(5) { z-index: 5; }
```

And footer: `z-index: 20`

But also, the kontak section is a sticky section with `height: 100vh` and `top: 0`. When all sticky sections stack at the top, the last one (kontak, z-index 5) is at the top of the viewport. But the footer, being positioned relative with z-index 20, would appear on top of it.

Wait, actually the issue might be more nuanced. The sticky sections all have `position: sticky; top: 0; height: 100vh;`. So they all stack at the top of the viewport, each covering the previous one. The kontak section (5th sticky) should be at the very top of the stack when you've scrolled all the way down. But then the footer comes after all the sticky sections in DOM order, and since it has `position: relative; z-index: 20`, it could be covering the kontak section.

Actually, wait. The sticky sections are all `position: sticky; top: 0; height: 100vh;`. When you scroll past all the content, all 5 sticky sections are "stuck" at the top, each covering the previous one. The footer is the next element after them. But the footer has `z-index: 20` and `position: relative`, which would make it appear above the sticky sections (z-index 1-5).

The fix: lower the footer z-index to something like 0, or increase the kontak section's z-index above 20. Or better yet, just remove the high z-index from the footer since it doesn't need to be that high.

